<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Tides and tsunami waves</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[[[if test="is(k = 1)"]]<p>At the end of a jetty in Kilindini harbour, Mombasa, the depth of the water is \(h\) metres, \(t\) hours after midnight, where</p><p>\[h = {@d@} + {@A@}\sin\left(30(t - {@t0@})\right)^\circ \quad\text{for } 0 \le t \le 24.\]</p><div>(a) Find the amplitude. [[input:ans1]] m [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) Find the period of the tide. [[input:ans2]] hours [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><div>(c) At what time, in hours after midnight, is the first high tide? [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>[[else]]<p>Far out in the Indian Ocean, the height \(h\) metres of a tsunami wave above normal sea level, at a distance \(x\) km along its path, is modelled by</p><p>\[h = {@A@}\sin({@bbd@}x)^\circ.\]</p><div>(a) Find the amplitude. [[input:ans1]] m [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><div>(b) Find the wavelength. [[input:ans2]] km [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><div>(c) How far along, in km, is the first crest? [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>[[/if]]]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[[[if test="is(k = 1)"]]<p>(a) The water rises \({@A@}\) m above its mean depth \({@d@}\) m: the amplitude is \({@A@}\) m.</p><p>(b) The angle grows by \(30^\circ\) every hour, and one complete wave is \(360^\circ\): \(360 \div 30 = 12\) hours. The graph is drawn against time, so the repeat length is a period.</p><p>(c) The depth is greatest where \(30(t - {@t0@}) = 90\), so \(t = {@t0@} + 3 = {@t0+3@}\)[[if test="is(t0 + 3 > 12)"]], or 12 hours earlier, \(t = {@fst@}\)[[/if]]. The first high tide is at \(t = {@fst@}\).</p>[[else]]<p>(a) The amplitude is \({@A@}\) m.</p><p>(b) The angle grows by \({@bbd@}^\circ\) every km, and one complete wave is \(360^\circ\): \(360 \div {@bbd@} = {@per@}\) km. The graph is drawn against distance, so the repeat length is a wavelength.</p><p>(c) The first crest is where \({@bbd@}x = 90\), so \(x = {@fst@}\) km, a quarter of the way along one wavelength.</p>[[/if]]]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: tides and tsunami waves. Kind 1: tide at Kilindini; kind 2: tsunami. Model numbers, not measurements. Source: original. */
L: [[1,1.5,2.1,7],[2,0.5,0,3/5],[1,1.3,1.9,1],[2,0.35,0,3/4],[1,1.6,2.2,2],[2,0.8,0,6/5],[1,1.4,2.0,4],[2,0.3,0,3/2],[1,1.8,2.4,5],[2,0.6,0,9/10]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
k: L[ix][1]; A: L[ix][2]; d: L[ix][3]; p: L[ix][4];
t0: p; bb: p; bbd: float(bb);
per: if k = 1 then 12 else 360/bb;
fst: if k = 1 then mod(3+t0, 12) else 90/bb;
dA1: 2*A; dA2: if k = 1 then A+d else -A;
dP1: if k = 1 then 30 else bb; dP2: per/2;
dF1: if k = 1 then t0 else per; dF2: if k = 1 then 3 else per/2; dF3: 90; dF4: if k = 1 then fst+6 else -fst;
nice(v) := block([r], r: floor(1000*v+1/2)/1000, if integerp(r) then r else float(r));
dFlate: fst+per;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
