    <node><name>1</name><description>Highest minus lowest</description><answertest>NumAbsolute</answertest><sans>ans1</sans><tans>dA1</tans><testoptions>0.001</testoptions><quiet>1</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt1-2-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>That is the difference between the highest and lowest levels. The amplitude is half of it.</p>]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>2</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt1-2-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
    <node><name>2</name><description>Greatest depth or trough</description><answertest>NumAbsolute</answertest><sans>ans1</sans><tans>dA2</tans><testoptions>0.001</testoptions><quiet>1</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt1-3-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[[[if test="is(k = 1)"]]<p>That is the greatest depth. The amplitude is how far the water rises above its mean depth, \({@d@}\) m.</p>[[else]]<p>A height below sea level gives the trough; the amplitude is a distance, so it is positive.</p>[[/if]]]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>-1</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt1-3-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[[[if test="is(k = 1)"]]<p>Test your value: with amplitude \({@ans1@}\) m the greatest depth would be \({@d@} + {@ans1@} = {@nice(d+ans1)@}\) m. Sine is never more than 1: put 1 for the sine in the model and compare.</p>[[else]]<p>Test your value: with amplitude \({@ans1@}\) m the highest crest would be \({@ans1@}\) m above normal sea level. Sine is never more than 1: put 1 for the sine in the model and compare.</p>[[/if]]]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
