    <node><name>3</name><description>Gave 90</description><answertest>NumAbsolute</answertest><sans>ans3</sans><tans>dF3</tans><testoptions>0.001</testoptions><quiet>1</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt3-4-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>90 is the angle where sine is greatest. Solve [[if test="is(k = 1)"]]\(30(t - {@t0@}) = 90\) for \(t\)[[else]]\({@bbd@}x = 90\) for \(x\)[[/if]].</p>]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>4</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt3-4-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
    <node><name>4</name><description>Low tide or negative distance</description><answertest>NumAbsolute</answertest><sans>ans3</sans><tans>dF4</tans><testoptions>0.001</testoptions><quiet>1</quiet><truescoremode>=</truescoremode><truescore>0.0000000</truescore><truepenalty></truepenalty><truenextnode>-1</truenextnode><trueanswernote>prt3-5-T</trueanswernote><truefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[[[if test="is(k = 1)"]]<p>That is a low tide, not a high tide.</p>[[else]]<p>Distance along the path is positive.</p>[[/if]]]]></text></truefeedback><falsescoremode>=</falsescoremode><falsescore>0.0000000</falsescore><falsepenalty></falsepenalty><falsenextnode>-1</falsenextnode><falseanswernote>prt3-5-F</falseanswernote><falsefeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[[[if test="latr"]]<p>That is a later [[if test="is(k = 1)"]]high tide[[else]]crest[[/if]], not the first one: there is an earlier one, one whole [[if test="is(k = 1)"]]period[[else]]wavelength[[/if]] before it.</p>[[else]]<p>Test your value: at [[if test="is(k = 1)"]]\(t = {@ans3@}\) the angle \(30(t - {@t0@})\)[[else]]\(x = {@ans3@}\) the angle \({@bbd@}x\)[[/if]] is \({@nice(angv)@}^\circ\). Sine is greatest when its angle is \(90^\circ\).</p>[[/if]]<p>Solve [[if test="is(k = 1)"]]\(30(t - {@t0@}) = 90\) for \(t\), then bring the time into \(0 \le t \le 12\)[[else]]\({@bbd@}x = 90\) for \(x\)[[/if]].</p>]]></text></falsefeedback></node>
